WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是詹娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金斯利。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.340
We were on The Office together.
我们一起出演过《办公室》。v

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们专门为你制作了《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们将剖析《办公室》的一集，并提供只有身临其境的两人才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是办公室女士。

8
00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:27.940
Hey, look at you, lady.
嘿，瞧瞧你，女士。

9
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:29.960
Look at me.
看着我。

10
00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:31.540
Yes, I'm looking at you.
是的，我在看你。

11
00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:32.740
I'm happy to see your face.
很高兴见到你的脸。

12
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:34.100
I'm wearing a new shirt.
我穿着一件新衬衫。

13
00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:35.460
You are.
你确实穿着。

14
00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:35.940
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

15
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:37.960
I'm getting into the button-downs.
我开始穿纽扣衬衫了。

16
00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:38.860
Finally.
总算。

17
00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:40.700
Can I just say finally?
我能说句终于吗？

18
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:41.520
Why?
为什么？

19
00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.720
Well, because I love a button-down.
嗯，因为我很喜欢纽扣衬衫。

20
00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:43.980
Oh.
哦。

21
00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:46.020
And now you're in the button-down club.
现在你也加入纽扣衬衫俱乐部了。

22
00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:46.920
I am.
我加入了。

23
00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.020
It's a wonderful place.
这是个好地方。

24
00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:51.340
Just wait till those flannel button-downs come into play.
等那些法兰绒纽扣衬衫派上用场的时候再说吧。

25
00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:52.560
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

26
00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:53.420
I know.
我知道。

27
00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.720
Well, today we're going to talk about The Boat.
好吧，今天我们要聊聊《那艘船》。

28
00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:03.740
It is Season 9, Episode 6, written by Dan Sterling and directed by John Krasinski.
这是第九季第六集，由丹·斯特林编剧，约翰·卡拉辛斯基执导。

29
00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.580
Do you know what the alternate title for this episode was?
你知道这一集的备用标题是什么吗？

30
00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:08.560
I'm going to guess.
我来猜猜。

31
00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:09.280
Okay.
好的。

32
00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:09.860
I don't know.
我不知道。

33
00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:10.720
I'm going to guess.
我来猜猜。

34
00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:12.920
Ah-ah-ahoy!
阿——阿——阿荷伊！

35
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:14.480
No.
不对。

36
00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:15.500
No, not.
不对，不是。

37
00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:15.920
Okay.
好吧。

38
00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:18.020
It was Andy's exit.
那是安迪的离开。

39
00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:19.340
Oh.
哦。

40
00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:20.920
You know, because he leaves.
你知道的，因为他离开了。

41
00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:21.280
Yes.
是的。

42
00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.780
He goes away in this episode.
他在这一集里离开了。

43
00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:26.380
Once again, Andy just leaves without giving any notice.
再说一次，安迪不打一声招呼就走了。

44
00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:27.780
He did this when he went to Florida.
他去佛罗里达州时就这样。

45
00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:28.540
What the heck?
搞什么鬼？

46
00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:32.360
Yes, and yet he's still the best candidate for manager?
是的，然而他仍然是经理的最佳人选？

47
00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:34.820
I just want to say Daryl's never gone anywhere.
我只想说达里尔从来没去过任何地方。

48
00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:35.800
No.
没有。

49
00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.380
Daryl has been there.
达里尔一直都在那儿。

50
00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.940
He hasn't started a business with a friend on the side.
他没有私下和朋友合伙开公司。

51
00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.440
He isn't also running a beet farm and owning the building.
他又没经营甜菜农场，也没买下整栋楼。

52
00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:50.180
I mean, I feel like if we could have anyone's complete focus as manager, Daryl is our candidate.
我是说，我觉得如果我们能让一个人百分之百专心当经理，达里尔就是我们的人选。

53
00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:53.780
And time and time again, he has great ideas.
而且一次又一次，他总是能提出很棒的想法。

54
00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:54.440
Yep.
没错。

55
00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.540
Well, here is your summary for The Boat.
好了，这是关于《那艘船》这一集的剧情总结。

56
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:04.840
Following a series of poor decisions by Mr. Bernard, the Bernard family finances are in ruin.
在伯纳德先生做出了一系列糟糕的决定后，伯纳德家族的财务状况彻底崩溃了。

57
00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:09.200
Andy attempts to salvage things by selling the family boat.
安迪试图通过卖掉家族的船来挽救局势。

58
00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:13.640
He's very sad, though, because he'd always dreamed of sailing it one day.
不过他非常难过，因为他一直梦想着有一天能亲自驾驶它出海。

59
00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:14.440
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

60
00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.880
Dwight is tricked into thinking he's being interviewed on the radio.
德怀特被忽悠了，以为自己正在接受电台采访。

61
00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:27.980
And finally, the burden of keeping Oscar's affair with the senator a secret falls squarely on Kevin's shoulders.
最后，保守奥斯卡和参议员有染这个秘密的重担，不偏不倚地落在了凯文的肩上。

62
00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.380
Kevin of all people.
偏偏是凯文。

63
00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:31.120
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

64
00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:33.740
I loved this particular storyline.
我特别喜欢这条故事线。

65
00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:34.535
I did, too.
我也一样。

66
00:02:34.535 --> 00:02:35.320
I loved it so much.
我太喜欢了。

67
00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:36.500
All right.
好的。

68
00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:39.400
Fast fact number one is a location breakdown.
趣味冷知识第一条是关于拍摄地点的。

69
00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:44.160
We got a fan question from Abby V in Knoxville, Tennessee, who said,
我们收到了来自田纳西州诺克斯维尔的粉丝艾比·V的提问，她问道：

70
00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:47.320
Where did you film the scenes with Aaron and Andy on the boat?
亚伦和安迪在船上的戏是在哪里拍的？

71
00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.820
Whose boat was it?
那是谁的船？

72
00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:49.940
Please tell us everything.
请把一切都告诉我们吧。

73
00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:55.340
Well, Abby V, because of Steve Burgess, I've got these answers for you.
好吧，艾比·V，多亏了史蒂夫·伯吉斯，我弄到了这些答案。

74
00:02:55.880 --> 00:03:00.200
We shot these scenes in Santa Monica at the Windjammers Yacht Club.
我们在圣莫尼卡的风向标游艇俱乐部拍摄了这些场景。

75
00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:03.280
We got the boat through our marine coordinator.
这艘船是通过我们的海上统筹找来的。

76
00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:05.080
He was a guy named Mike George.
那是个叫迈克·乔治的家伙。

77
00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:10.840
He was also a friend of our first AD, Kelly Cantley, because, you know, she sails boats.
他也是我们第一副导演凯莉·坎特利的女性朋友，因为，你知道的，她会开船。

78
00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:11.500
Yeah.
是啊。

79
00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:16.480
Steve Burgess said that it was so perfect that she was the first AD for this episode.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说，她能担任这一集的第一副导演简直太完美了。

80
00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:21.840
She really helped us with the boat stuff, particularly the parts where the boat had to be moving.
她确实在船只方面帮了我们大忙，尤其是船需要移动的那些镜头。

81
00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:27.780
So, I reached out to Kelly to ask her more specifics about this episode.
所以，我联系了凯莉，向她询问关于这一集的更多细节。

82
00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:29.740
She was wonderful.
她人太好了。

83
00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.360
So much detail.
提供了好多的细节。

84
00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:32.180
You want to hear it?
你想听吗？

85
00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:33.360
I do.
我想听。

86
00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:40.260
She said that we scouted a few available boats, and we had a very specific criteria.
她说我们考察了几艘现成的船，而且我们有非常具体的要求。

87
00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:47.660
We needed a boat that was big enough where we could shoot down below, but also small enough
我们需要一艘足够大的船，大到我们能在船舱下面拍摄，但同时又不能太大

88
00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:51.800
that Ed could actually sail it by himself, that it would be realistic.
要让安迪真的能独自驾驭它，这样才显得逼真。

89
00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:52.740
Yeah.
对。

90
00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:58.380
We also needed it to look luxurious enough for the Bernard family to have owned it.
我们还要求它看起来足够奢华，符合伯纳德家族曾经拥有的身份。

91
00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:04.300
She said we rented a boat from a yacht broker, and this boat technically could not have been
她说我们是从一个游艇经纪人那里租了一艘船，这艘船严格来说不可能

92
00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:09.040
in Andy's family since before he was born, but it was a pretty good match for ones of
在安迪出生前就已经是他们家的了，但它跟那个时期的船

93
00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:09.720
that time.
匹配度相当高。

94
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.000
So, I guess a little bit of a cheat there.
所以，我猜这里面有点小小的穿帮作弊吧。

95
00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:14.360
I wonder if there's some, like,
我在想会不会有一些，比如说，

96
00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:16.900
boat people out there who saw that.
懂船的人看了那一幕。

97
00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:18.200
When they saw the episode, they were like,
当他们看到那一集的时候，心想：

98
00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:20.180
there's no way that's been in their family that long.
这船绝对不可能在他们家待那么久。

99
00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:21.020
That's a new boat.
那明明是一艘新船。

100
00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:24.780
A hundred percent, because if you're a boat person, you know everything about boats.
百分之百是的，因为如果你是个懂船的人，你对船的事情无所不知。

101
00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:27.760
Kind of like you and trains.
有点像你和火车。

102
00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:30.540
I don't know everything about trains.
我对火车并不是无所不知。

103
00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:31.480
I just like trains.
我只是喜欢火车。

104
00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:32.940
But let me tell you,
不过我跟你说，

105
00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:39.760
the fun person to sit at, like, a dinner party is someone that, like, loves boats or trains.
晚宴上那种坐着最有意思的人，就是那种，比如说，超级热爱船只或火车的人。

106
00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:41.220
Oh, I beg to differ.
哦，恕我不敢苟同。

107
00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:43.020
Or perhaps hummingbirds.
或者也许是蜂鸟。

108
00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:44.780
I want to sit next to those people.
我想坐在那些人旁边。

109
00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:46.920
I want to hear all your boat stories.
我想听你讲所有关于船的故事。

110
00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:47.840
Okay.
好吧。

111
00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:50.100
Jenna does not.
珍娜可不想。

112
00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:56.700
I mean, maybe, maybe, maybe not.
我是说，也许吧，也许会，也许不会。

113
00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:58.220
You know what?
你知道吗？

114
00:04:58.320 --> 00:04:59.360
Jenna would do the nod.
珍娜会点头敷衍。

115
00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.640
It's coming up in the whale in the next episode.
在下一集的鲸鱼桥段里就会出现。

116
00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:03.640
You would be doing, like, the Dwight nod.
你就会做出那种，呃，德怀特式的点头。

117
00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:05.140
Yes, I am listening.
是的，我在听。

118
00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:06.980
It's true.
千真万确。

119
00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:10.160
Kelly said this was not the only boat.
凯莉说过这可不是唯一的船。

120
00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:12.780
We were a little bit, like, speed here.
我们当时有点像，赶进度。

121
00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:13.180
It's
并不是

122
00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:16.860
not that we had a bunch of different, like, main picture boats.
我们有各种各样不同的那种主要拍摄用船。

123
00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:18.200
We only had that one.
我们只有那一艘。

124
00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:20.200
We didn't have 13 boats.
我们可没有13艘船。

125
00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:21.060
We did not.
确实没有。

126
00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.540
But we had a lot of support boats.
但我们有很多支援船。

127
00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:27.580
She said we had, yeah, I know, support boats.
她说我们有，对，我知道，支援船。

128
00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:28.320
That's so sweet.
太贴心了。

129
00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:29.900
Yeah, little support boats.
对，小支援船。

130
00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.940
We had two pontoon boats for lighting the dock.
我们有两艘浮桥船用来给码头照明。

131
00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:37.420
And we had two inflatable ribs for camera and crew transfer.
我们还有两艘充气刚性艇用于摄像机和剧组人员的转移。

132
00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:46.960
We had a seven-person marine crew, a marine coordinator, sail masters, a lifeguard, and support boat drivers.
我们有一个七人的水上工作组，一名水上统筹、帆船大师、救生员以及支援船驾驶员。

133
00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:52.780
So it was like a whole second marine crew to pull off this episode.
所以为了完成这一集，简直就像又多了一个水上工作组。

134
00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:55.520
Yeah, it was like the main boat and his buddies.
对，就像是主船和它的好哥们儿。

135
00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:57.620
Exactly, lady.
一点没错，美女。

136
00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:02.320
And, you know, of course, there were a ton of safety meetings.
而且，当然啦，还有成堆的安全会议。

137
00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:03.600
Oh, yes.
哦，是的。

138
00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:10.160
There was a full-page safety memo that went out to the cast and crew.
有一份整整一页的安全备忘录发给了演员和剧组人员。

139
00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:10.880
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

140
00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:12.840
It was extensive.
内容非常详尽。

141
00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:15.540
It was so detailed.
极其详细。

142
00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:16.780
You and I both read it.
你和我两个人都读了。

143
00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:19.540
And some of the things on there cracked me up.
上面有些内容把我逗乐了。

144
00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:21.260
Oh, it's very funny.
哦，非常有意思。

145
00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:23.320
Wait, I want to share a few, okay?
等等，我想分享几个，好吗？

146
00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:24.320
And then you share some.
然后你也分享几个。

147
00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:24.720
Okay.
好。

148
00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:32.420
So some of these safety measures, Jenna, just the way they were listed and phrased cracked me up
所以其中一些安全措施，珍娜，光是它们被列出来和措辞的方式就把我逗笑了，

149
00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:38.680
because it reminded me of a memo we might get from, like, a second-grade school teacher on what to do on a field trip.
因为它让我想起了一份我们可能会收到的备忘录，比如来自小学老师关于春游该做什么的叮嘱。

150
00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:40.380
Yes, so much.
对，非常有这种感觉。

151
00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:40.940
Ready?
准备好了吗？

152
00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.720
Here were the three that really made me chuckle.
以下是让我真正忍不住发笑的三条。

153
00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:49.100
Number one, number one on the list, use a lot of sunblock.
第一条，也是清单上的第一条，多涂防晒霜。

154
00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:50.260
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

155
00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:54.760
Number two, if you are feeling seasick, please let the medic know.
第二条，如果你感到晕船，请告知医护人员。

156
00:06:55.380 --> 00:07:01.960
Number three, if you need to throw up, please do so over the side of the boat and not in the boat.
第三条，如果你需要呕吐，请在船舷外吐，不要吐在船舱里。

157
00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:03.160
Yes.
没错。

158
00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:07.520
There were so many instructions for what to do should you might vomit.
上面有那么多关于万一你想呕吐该怎么做的指示。

159
00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:13.900
Well, what was interesting is it was very clear to me from this memo how protective they were of the boat.
嗯，有趣的是，从这份备忘录里我很清楚地看出他们有多爱护这艘船。

160
00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:18.800
There were, like, three different ways that they told you not to ruin the boat.
他们大概用三种不同的方式提醒你不要弄坏这艘船。

161
00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:22.200
It was like, if you have to throw up, don't throw up in the boat.
就像是，如果你非吐不可，别吐在船上。

162
00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:22.440
Exactly.
正是。

163
00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:23.980
Throw up on the side of the boat.
吐在船舷外。

164
00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:24.400
Yeah.
对。

165
00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:28.460
And then there are a lot of mention of don't scratch the boat.
然后里面还大量提到了不要刮伤船。

166
00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:34.260
Clip your radio to your body in such a way that it won't accidentally scratch the boat.
把对讲机别在身上，注意别不小心刮伤船。

167
00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:38.040
Don't wear belt buckles because we don't want to scratch the boat.
不要系皮带扣，因为我们不想刮伤船。

168
00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:39.860
And I asked Kelly about it.
我问了凯莉这件事。

169
00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:43.840
I was like, Kelly, what is with these multiple instructions about not scratching the boat?
我说，凯莉，这上面怎么有这么多关于不要刮伤船的指示？

170
00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:51.680
And she said that the gel coat and wood trim on a boat is, like, very susceptible to scratches and dings.
她说船上的胶衣和木质饰条非常容易产生划痕和凹痕。

171
00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:56.000
And the yacht broker who rented us the boat was watching us.
把船租给我们的游艇经纪人一直在盯着我们。

172
00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.420
And we didn't want to have to pay for any repairs.
而且我们不想支付任何维修费用。

173
00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:02.920
So they were, like, telling everyone to be super duper duper careful.
所以他们就像是在叮嘱每个人务必、务必、务必小心。

174
00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:04.700
Protect the boat.
保护好船。

175
00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:07.740
Protect the boat at all costs, but also wear your sunblock.
不惜一切代价保护这艘船，但也别忘了涂防晒霜。

176
00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:08.840
All right.
行吧。

177
00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:10.540
Those are your boat facts, folks.
各位，以上就是你们的游艇冷知识。

178
00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:12.760
Are you ready for fast fact number two?
准备好听第二个快速冷知识了吗？

179
00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:13.500
Yeah.
好啊。

180
00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:14.660
Okay.
好的。

181
00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:20.080
There was a super amazing thing that was happening the week they were scouting this location.
就在他们勘测这个外景地的那个星期，发生了一件超级了不起的事。

182
00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:21.920
So they're out at the dock.
当时他们正在码头上。

183
00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:23.400
They're looking at boats.
他们在看船。

184
00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:24.400
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

185
00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:27.260
And do you remember this moment in history, Angela?
安吉拉，你还记得历史上的这个时刻吗？

186
00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:29.040
This is, like, Los Angeles history.
这可以说是洛杉矶的历史。

187
00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:31.560
The space shuttle Endeavor.
“奋进号”航天飞机。

188
00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:32.600
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

189
00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:41.160
Which they put on top of a 747 airplane because they were transporting it from Florida to the Los Angeles Science Center where it was going to be on display.
他们把它背在一架波音747飞机顶部，因为它要从佛罗里达运送到洛杉矶科学中心去展出。

190
00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:44.220
It flew over their heads.
它从他们的头顶飞过。

191
00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:45.680
That's so cool, right?
太酷了，对吧？

192
00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:46.800
Do you remember this?
你还记得这个吗？

193
00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:47.840
Of course.
当然记得。

194
00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:50.300
Everyone in Los Angeles was abuzz about this.
洛杉矶的每个人当时都在热烈讨论这事。

195
00:08:50.700 --> 00:09:06.180
You know the part I remember is how once it landed at the airport, they then had to get it all the way through the busy, narrow streets of Los Angeles to the giant,
我记得最清楚的一部分是，它在机场降落后，他们必须把它穿过洛杉矶繁忙而狭窄的街道，运到那个巨大的……

196
00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:11.200
I don't know what you call it, the giant aircraft hangar where it now sits, where you can go with your kids.
我不知道该怎么称呼它，就是那个巨大的飞机机库，它现在就停在那儿，你可以带着孩子去参观。

197
00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:14.580
I was a chaperone for the year my daughter's school went.
我女儿学校去的那年我是随队家长。

198
00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:19.380
It was their trip in first grade, and we went and saw the space shuttle, and I was a chaperone.
那是他们一年级的春游，我们去看了航天飞机，我是带队家长。

199
00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:21.960
It's so, so amazing.
真的太神奇了。

200
00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:23.940
If you're in Los Angeles, you have to go see it.
如果你在洛杉矶，你一定要去看看。

201
00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:28.060
But the journey to get it there was so cool.
但把这东西运到那里的过程真是太酷了。

202
00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:30.600
It was so crazy, and I completely remember it.
当时太疯狂了，我记得清清楚楚。

203
00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:31.440
I looked it up.
我特意查了一下。

204
00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:35.900
They had to temporarily remove or raise up traffic lights.
他们不得不临时移走或抬高交通信号灯。

205
00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:36.480
Yes.
是的。

206
00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:46.540
They had to remove 400 trees along the side of the road to make room, but they pledged to replace each removed tree with four new trees.
为了腾出空间，他们不得不砍掉路边的400棵树，但他们承诺每砍一棵树就补种四棵新树。

207
00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:49.940
So I guess we got 1,600 trees in the end.
所以我想我们最后多出了1600棵树。

208
00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:58.120
But the thing that I remember is that at the time, my family was living up in the hills, and we had a big kitchen window,
但我记得当时我家人住在山上，我们有一个很大的厨房窗户，

209
00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:03.360
and we had made a makeshift changing station for my son in the kitchen.
我们在厨房里为我儿子弄了一个简易的换尿布台。

210
00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:09.240
So if we were upstairs in the house, which is where the kitchen was, we could change him easily.
所以如果我们楼上在房子里，也就是厨房所在的那层，我们就能很方便地给他换尿布。

211
00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:10.400
You know, you do that.
你知道的，你都会这么做。

212
00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:11.380
Yeah, yeah, sure.
对，对，当然。

213
00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:17.840
So I was changing him on this little changing table, and it flew past our window.
所以我正给他在这个小换尿布台上换尿布，它就从我们窗前飞过去了。

214
00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:19.620
That's so wild.
太疯狂了。

215
00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:23.820
And I went, and I tried to grab my phone, but I didn't get it in time to take a picture.
然后我赶紧去拿手机，但没来得及拍下照片。

216
00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:25.140
But I was like, oh, my God.
当时我心里想，天哪。

217
00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:30.180
And then, of course, it was crazy because a couple years later, I took him there so that he could see it.
然后，当然，最疯狂的是几年后我带他去那儿参观，好让他能亲眼看看。

218
00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:31.180
Yeah.
对。

219
00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:34.460
Yeah, it's a really great visit if you're in Los Angeles.
对，如果你在洛杉矶的话，去那儿参观真的很棒。

220
00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:42.860
You know, the other thing is if you go to see the space shuttle, they have this great, I don't know what you call it,
你知道的，还有一件事是，如果你去看航天飞机，他们有一个很棒的——我不知道该怎么称呼它——

221
00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:47.820
like a mini documentary of getting it to the big aircraft hangar.
就像是一个关于把它运到那个巨大飞机机库的迷你纪录片。

222
00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:52.680
What all it took, what all, and then how people, like, line the streets to see it.
运送它付出了多少努力，以及人们是如何排着长队去观看的。

223
00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:53.080
Yeah.
对。

224
00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:56.680
And I remember it was like the evening news, like every day I'd be like, where is it now?
我记得当时就像晚间新闻一样，每天我都会想：它现在到哪儿了？

225
00:10:57.060 --> 00:10:57.320
Yeah.
对。

226
00:10:57.480 --> 00:10:58.560
On the TV, where is it now?
在电视上，它现在到哪儿了？

227
00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:00.320
I totally remember it.
我完全记得。

228
00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:02.020
Wow, and that was going on.
哇，而且这事正好发生在那会儿。

229
00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:04.000
During the prep of this episode.
在我们为这期节目做准备的时候。

230
00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:09.340
All right, moving on to fast fact number three, fan question from Logan B.
好了，接下来是第三个快速冷知识，来自北卡罗来纳州的洛根·B的粉丝提问，

231
00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:13.120
in North Carolina, and many other people wrote in about this as well.
还有许多其他人也写信问了这个问题。

232
00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:18.060
Logan said, I noticed that Andrew Santino is in this episode.
洛根说，我注意到安德鲁·桑蒂诺在这集节目里。

233
00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:23.140
His podcast is so funny, and I would love to hear about his time on the show.
他的播客太搞笑了，我很想听听他在这档节目里的经历。

234
00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:29.220
Yes, everybody, the grumpy sailor from the boat.
没错，各位，就是那个船上脾气暴躁的水手。

235
00:11:29.340 --> 00:11:30.220
In the big sweater.
穿着大毛衣的那个。

236
00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:34.840
Yes, is actor and comedian Andrew Santino.
对，他就是演员兼喜剧演员安德鲁·桑蒂诺。

237
00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:36.800
He actually has two podcasts.
他其实有两个播客。

238
00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:42.020
He has Whiskey Ginger, where he interviews friends while they sip whiskey.
一个是《威士忌姜》，他在节目里边品威士忌边采访朋友。

239
00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:43.800
Um, hello.
嗯，你好。

240
00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:45.020
Yes.
对。

241
00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:45.360
Hello.
你好。

242
00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:46.240
Give us a call.
给我们打个电话吧。

243
00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:46.880
Yeah.
对。

244
00:11:47.380 --> 00:11:48.160
Up for it.
奉陪到底。

245
00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:55.420
And he also has the podcast Bad Friends, which he co-hosts with Bobby Lee, who was my co-star on Splitting Up Together.
而且他还有个播客叫《坏朋友》，是和鲍比·李共同主持的，鲍比曾是我在《离婚再一起》里的联合主演。

246
00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:56.200
What?
什么？

247
00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:58.100
We have a Splitting Up Together crossover.
我们来了一次《离婚再一起》的梦幻联动。

248
00:11:58.620 --> 00:11:59.220
We do.
确实如此。

249
00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:02.400
So, I slid into Andrew's DMs.
所以，我私信了安德鲁。

250
00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:04.160
We haven't done that in a while, Ange.
我们好久没这么干过了，安吉。

251
00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:05.520
Did a little DM slide.
我发了一条私信。

252
00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:06.160
I know.
我知道。

253
00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:06.720
I know.
我知道。

254
00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:08.620
And he was kind enough to respond.
他也很友善地回复了。

255
00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:10.120
He sent us audio clips.
他给我们发了音频片段。

256
00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:11.660
They're very funny.
它们非常搞笑。

257
00:12:11.780 --> 00:12:12.960
I can't wait for you to share them.
我迫不及待想让你分享出来。

258
00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:13.800
Of course.
当然。

259
00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:16.740
We had to ask him, how did he get his job on The Office?
我们不得不问他，他是怎么得到《办公室》这份工作的？

260
00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:19.040
And was he a fan of the show?
他以前是这部剧的粉丝吗？

261
00:12:19.220 --> 00:12:20.300
Here's what he had to say.
他是这么说的。

262
00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:27.240
Allison Jones was the casting director, became a huge fan of mine from all my other failed auditions that I did for her.
艾莉森·琼斯是选角导演，她通过我以前所有那些失败的试镜对我有了一个深刻的印象。

263
00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:30.920
And she was like, I think I've got something perfect for you.
她说，我觉得我这里有个非常适合你的角色。

264
00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:37.420
It's a minimal amount of lines, but you have to look like a sloppy sailor in an oversized sweater.
台词非常少，但你得看起来像个穿着超大号毛衣、邋里邋遢的水手。

265
00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:38.760
And I said, sign me up.
我说，算我一个。

266
00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:39.380
That's perfect.
太完美了。

267
00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:41.360
And so, yeah, I did just audition.
所以，是的，我确实去试镜了。

268
00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:43.920
And I got it, and I was extremely excited.
然后我拿到了角色，我当时超级激动。

269
00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:47.780
It was like the first big job I had ever had on a massive network television show.
那可以说是我在大型电视网剧集里接到的第一份大工作。

270
00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:50.780
And to answer the second question, of course, I was familiar with the show.
至于回答第二个问题，我当然对这部剧很熟悉。

271
00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:52.000
I was a massive fan of the show.
我是这部剧的超级粉丝。

272
00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:57.480
Being a stand-up comedian, I was a fan of the British office, the OG office.
作为一名单口喜剧演员，我是英版《办公室》、原版《办公室》的粉丝。

273
00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:59.320
Do I think the American one is better?
我觉得美版更好吗？

274
00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:00.240
I don't know.
我不知道。

275
00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:02.080
That's not for me to say, but it is.
这不是我能评价的，但它确实更好。

276
00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:04.400
But no, I like them both just the same.
不过说真的，两部我都一样喜欢。

277
00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:06.040
They're both very good.
它们都非常棒。

278
00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:08.220
But I was a huge fan.
但我真的是个超级粉丝。

279
00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:10.760
Good old Allison Jones.
好样的，艾莉森·琼斯。

280
00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:13.060
Once again, finding us great people.
她再次为我们找来了这么棒的人。

281
00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:13.880
I know.
我知道。

282
00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:18.720
So I had to ask him, since this was one of his first jobs,
所以我不得不问他，既然这是他最早的工作之一，

283
00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:26.520
what was it like for him to show up on set and be directed by John Krasinski and then be in a scene with this group of actors?
他第一次来到片场，接受约翰·卡拉辛斯基的执导，然后和这群演员一起拍戏，是一种什么样的体验？

284
00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:28.060
Here's what he said.
他是这么说的。

285
00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:30.340
He was extremely mean and rude.
他极其尖酸刻薄。

286
00:13:30.460 --> 00:13:32.040
He would throw stuff at us in between takes.
拍戏间隙他会朝我们扔东西。

287
00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:33.560
If you messed up, he would yell at you.
如果你演砸了，他就会对你大吼大叫。

288
00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:35.840
He would give you intense stare-downs.
他会恶狠狠地盯着你。

289
00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:39.280
A very, very mean, rude man, and I will never work with him again.
一个非常非常刻薄粗鲁的人，我再也不会跟他合作了。

290
00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:40.900
He was wonderful.
他太棒了。

291
00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:42.240
He was really cool.
他真的很酷。

292
00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:48.560
And I think I told him it was one of my first jobs, so he was really nice about it and was really easy to work with.
我想我告诉过他这是我的第一份工作之一，所以他对此人非常好，合作起来也很轻松。

293
00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:50.560
And Groban was on that one, The Grobesters.
而且格罗班也在那集里，就是那个格罗贝斯特人。

294
00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:51.920
So it was cool.
所以这很酷。

295
00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:52.740
It was really fun.
真的非常有趣。

296
00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:53.860
And he was really nice and easy.
而且他真的很好、很随和。

297
00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:56.540
And to be honest, my scene wasn't too complex.
说实话，我的戏份并不算太复杂。

298
00:13:57.860 --> 00:14:01.000
So smacking Ed Helms was about the depth of how far I needed to go.
所以扇埃德·赫尔姆斯耳光基本上就是我需要达到的表演深度了。

299
00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:02.380
And Ellie was cool.
艾莉也很酷。

300
00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:03.620
Everyone was very nice to me.
每个人对我都非常好。

301
00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:09.140
But truly, it was such a cool experience to have, like, that be my first debut in network television.
但说实话，这真的是一种很酷的体验，可以说是我的电视网首秀。

302
00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:11.020
So cool.
太酷了。

303
00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:12.560
After her?
在她之后？

304
00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:13.340
Yeah.
对。

305
00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:15.100
That's awesome.
太棒了。

306
00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:19.340
Is it just me, or does it sound like Andrew is driving down the freeway?
